1
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:06,817
Water, earth,

2
00:00:06,901 --> 00:00:10,195
fire, air...

3
00:00:11,322 --> 00:00:15,367
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

4
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:18,745
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

5
00:00:19,789 --> 00:00:23,709
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

6
00:00:23,793 --> 00:00:25,627
But when the world needed him most,

7
00:00:25,712 --> 00:00:27,004
he vanished.

8
00:00:27,422 --> 00:00:31,216
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

9
00:00:31,301 --> 00:00:32,884
an airbender named Aang.

10
00:00:32,969 --> 00:00:35,262
And although his
airbending skills are great,

11
00:00:35,346 --> 00:00:38,015
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

12
00:00:38,975 --> 00:00:42,269
But I believe Aang can save the world.

13
00:01:14,927 --> 00:01:17,262
The only reason
you should be interrupting me

14
00:01:17,347 --> 00:01:20,057
is if you have news about the Avatar.

15
00:01:20,141 --> 00:01:22,267
Well, there is news, Prince Zuko,

16
00:01:22,352 --> 00:01:23,894
but you might not like it.

17
00:01:23,978 --> 00:01:25,020
Don't get too upset.

18
00:01:25,104 --> 00:01:27,898
Uncle, you taught me that
keeping a level head

19
00:01:27,982 --> 00:01:29,524
is a sign of a great leader.

20
00:01:29,609 --> 00:01:32,110
Now, whatever you have to say,
I'm sure I can take it.

21
00:01:32,653 --> 00:01:34,112
Ok, then.

22
00:01:34,197 --> 00:01:36,281
We have no idea where he is.

23
00:01:36,366 --> 00:01:37,574
What?

24
00:01:38,618 --> 00:01:41,036
You really should open a window
in here.

25
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,287
Give me the map!

26
00:01:42,372 --> 00:01:45,791
There have been multiple sightings
of the Avatar,

27
00:01:45,875 --> 00:01:48,668
but he is impossible to track down.

28
00:01:48,753 --> 00:01:50,212
How am I going to find him, Uncle?

29
00:01:50,296 --> 00:01:53,340
He is clearly a master
of evasive maneuvering.

30
00:01:55,218 --> 00:01:57,552
You have no idea
where you're going, do you?

31
00:01:57,637 --> 00:01:59,429
Well, I know it's near water.

32
00:02:00,515 --> 00:02:02,516
I guess
we're getting close, then.

33
00:02:04,936 --> 00:02:06,645
Momo, marbles, please.

34
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:12,234
Hey, Katara, check out
this airbending trick.

35
00:02:15,655 --> 00:02:16,947
That's great, Aang.

36
00:02:17,031 --> 00:02:19,574
You didn't even look.

37
00:02:19,659 --> 00:02:20,867
That's great.

38
00:02:20,952 --> 00:02:22,244
But I'm not doing it now.

39
00:02:22,328 --> 00:02:23,787
Stop bugging her, airhead.

40
00:02:23,871 --> 00:02:26,039
You need to give girls space
when they do their sewing.

41
00:02:26,165 --> 00:02:29,584
What does me being a girl
have to do with sewing?

42
00:02:29,669 --> 00:02:30,836
Simple.

43
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,379
Girls are better
at fixing pants than guys,

44
00:02:32,463 --> 00:02:34,714
and guys are better at hunting
and fighting and stuff like that.

45
00:02:34,799 --> 00:02:36,425
It's just the natural order of things.

46
00:02:36,509 --> 00:02:37,717
All done with your pants,

47
00:02:37,802 --> 00:02:39,928
and look what a great job I did.

48
00:02:42,181 --> 00:02:43,765
Wait! I was just kidding!

49
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:46,101
I can't wear these! Katara, please!

50
00:02:46,227 --> 00:02:47,436
Relax, Sokka.

51
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:49,604
Where we're going,
you won't need any pants.

52
00:02:55,445 --> 00:02:57,279
We just made
a pit stop yesterday.

53
00:02:57,363 --> 00:02:59,531
Shouldn't we get a little more flying
done before we camp out?

54
00:03:00,241 --> 00:03:01,616
He's right. At this rate,

55
00:03:01,701 --> 00:03:03,535
we won't get to the North Pole
until spring.

56
00:03:03,619 --> 00:03:05,036
But Appa's tired already,

57
00:03:05,121 --> 00:03:06,580
aren't you, boy?

58
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:10,625
I said, "Aren't you, boy?"

59
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:15,005
Yeah, that was real convincing.

60
00:03:15,089 --> 00:03:17,924
Still, hard to argue
with a 10-ton magical monster.

61
00:03:18,342 --> 00:03:19,342
Look!

62
00:03:23,181 --> 00:03:25,765
That's why we're here... Elephant koi,

63
00:03:25,850 --> 00:03:27,142
and I'm going to ride it.

64
00:03:27,226 --> 00:03:28,977
Katara, you've got to watch me.

65
00:03:32,899 --> 00:03:34,524
Cold!

66
00:03:48,372 --> 00:03:49,498
Woo!

67
00:03:49,582 --> 00:03:51,500
Yeah!

68
00:03:55,838 --> 00:03:56,963
Woo-hoo!

69
00:03:59,050 --> 00:04:00,509
He looks pretty good out there.

70
00:04:00,593 --> 00:04:03,094
Are you kidding?
The fish is doing all the work.

71
00:04:03,888 --> 00:04:05,096
No, Appa!

72
00:04:05,181 --> 00:04:06,389
Don't eat that!

73
00:04:12,104 --> 00:04:13,522
Aw, man.

74
00:04:18,027 --> 00:04:19,277
There's something in the water!

75
00:04:24,283 --> 00:04:25,367
What's wrong?

76
00:04:25,451 --> 00:04:26,493
Aang's in trouble.

77
00:04:26,577 --> 00:04:28,286
-Aang!
-Get out of there!

78
00:04:29,497 --> 00:04:31,831
-Get back here, Aang!
-Come in!

79
00:04:39,757 --> 00:04:40,757
Aah!

80
00:04:54,897 --> 00:04:56,439
What was that thing?

81
00:04:56,524 --> 00:04:57,649
I don't know.

82
00:04:57,733 --> 00:04:59,401
Well, let's not stick around
to find out.

83
00:04:59,485 --> 00:05:00,944
Time to hit the road.

84
00:05:12,498 --> 00:05:14,624
Or we could stay a while.

85
00:05:19,297 --> 00:05:22,215
You three have some
explaining to do.

86
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:24,426
And if you don't answer
all our questions,

87
00:05:24,510 --> 00:05:26,803
we're throwing you back
in the water with the unagi.

88
00:05:26,887 --> 00:05:28,847
Show yourselves, cowards!

89
00:05:31,767 --> 00:05:34,269
Who are you?
Where are the men who ambushed us?

90
00:05:34,353 --> 00:05:36,563
There were no men. We ambushed you.

91
00:05:36,647 --> 00:05:39,274
Now tell us, who are you
and what are you doing here?

92
00:05:39,358 --> 00:05:40,442
Wait a second.

93
00:05:40,526 --> 00:05:42,611
There's no way a bunch of girls
took us down.

94
00:05:42,695 --> 00:05:44,571
A bunch of girls?

95
00:05:44,655 --> 00:05:47,073
The unagi's going to eat well tonight.

96
00:05:47,158 --> 00:05:49,117
No, don't hurt him! He didn't mean it!

97
00:05:49,201 --> 00:05:51,328
My brother's just an idiot sometimes.

98
00:05:52,121 --> 00:05:53,788
It's my fault.

99
00:05:53,873 --> 00:05:55,040
I'm sorry we came here.

100
00:05:55,124 --> 00:05:56,583
I wanted to ride the elephant koi.

101
00:05:56,667 --> 00:06:00,086
How do we know
you're not Fire Nation spies?

102
00:06:00,171 --> 00:06:02,505
Kyoshi stayed out of the war so far

103
00:06:02,590 --> 00:06:04,633
and we intend to keep it that way.

104
00:06:04,717 --> 00:06:07,052
This island is named for Kyoshi?

105
00:06:07,136 --> 00:06:08,261
I know Kyoshi.

106
00:06:08,346 --> 00:06:09,512
Ha!

107
00:06:09,597 --> 00:06:11,264
How could you possibly know her?

108
00:06:11,349 --> 00:06:15,727
Avatar Kyoshi was born here
400 years ago.

109
00:06:15,811 --> 00:06:17,812
She's been dead for centuries.

110
00:06:19,315 --> 00:06:21,691
I know her because I'm the Avatar.

111
00:06:21,776 --> 00:06:23,068
That's impossible.

112
00:06:23,152 --> 00:06:26,571
The last Avatar was an airbender
who disappeared 100 years ago.

113
00:06:26,656 --> 00:06:27,656
That's me.

114
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:29,991
Throw the impostor to the unagi.

115
00:06:33,412 --> 00:06:35,872
Aang, do some airbending.

116
00:06:38,668 --> 00:06:40,835
- Wow.
- That's amazing.

117
00:06:42,838 --> 00:06:44,130
It's true.

118
00:06:44,215 --> 00:06:46,174
You are the Avatar.

119
00:06:46,258 --> 00:06:48,510
Now, check this out.

120
00:06:57,478 --> 00:06:58,978
Did you hear the news?

121
00:06:59,063 --> 00:07:00,689
The Avatar's on Kyoshi.

122
00:07:10,533 --> 00:07:12,283
The Avatar's on Kyoshi island?

123
00:07:13,077 --> 00:07:14,869
Uncle, ready the rhinos.

124
00:07:14,954 --> 00:07:16,913
He's not getting away from me
this time.

125
00:07:16,997 --> 00:07:18,998
Are you going to finish that?

126
00:07:19,083 --> 00:07:21,000
I was going to save it for later!

127
00:07:39,854 --> 00:07:41,146
All right!

128
00:07:41,230 --> 00:07:42,522
Dessert for breakfast!

129
00:07:42,732 --> 00:07:46,317
These people sure know
how to treat an Avatar.

130
00:07:46,402 --> 00:07:48,445
Katara, you've got to try these.

131
00:07:48,529 --> 00:07:50,155
Well, maybe just a bite.

132
00:07:52,658 --> 00:07:54,284
Sokka, what's your problem?

133
00:07:54,368 --> 00:07:55,410
Eat!

134
00:07:55,494 --> 00:07:56,494
I'm not hungry.

135
00:07:56,704 --> 00:07:58,329
But you're always hungry.

136
00:07:58,414 --> 00:08:00,790
He's just upset
because a bunch of girls

137
00:08:00,875 --> 00:08:02,333
kicked his butt yesterday.

138
00:08:02,418 --> 00:08:03,585
They snuck up on me!

139
00:08:03,669 --> 00:08:05,879
Right, and then they kicked your butt.

140
00:08:06,297 --> 00:08:08,214
Sneak attacks don't count.

141
00:08:08,299 --> 00:08:09,883
Tie me up with ropes...

142
00:08:09,967 --> 00:08:12,010
I'll show them a thing or two.

143
00:08:12,094 --> 00:08:13,803
I'm not scared of any girls.

144
00:08:13,888 --> 00:08:15,930
Who do they think they are, anyway?

145
00:08:16,015 --> 00:08:17,891
This is tasty.

146
00:08:18,517 --> 00:08:20,477
What's he so angry about?

147
00:08:20,561 --> 00:08:21,603
It's great here.

148
00:08:21,687 --> 00:08:23,188
They're giving us the royal treatment.

149
00:08:23,397 --> 00:08:25,106
Hey, don't get too comfortable.

150
00:08:25,191 --> 00:08:27,776
It's risky for us to stay
in one place for very long.

151
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:29,319
I'm sure we'll be fine.

152
00:08:29,403 --> 00:08:32,030
Besides, did you see how happy
I'm making this town?

153
00:08:32,114 --> 00:08:34,157
They're even cleaning up
that statue in my honor.

154
00:08:34,241 --> 00:08:37,660
Well, it's nice to see you excited
about being the Avatar.

155
00:08:37,745 --> 00:08:39,454
I just hope it doesn't
all go to your head.

156
00:08:39,663 --> 00:08:41,539
Come on, you know me better than that.

157
00:08:41,624 --> 00:08:43,416
I'm just a simple monk.

158
00:08:44,877 --> 00:08:46,753
There he is!

159
00:08:46,837 --> 00:08:48,963
There he is!!

160
00:09:09,401 --> 00:09:11,945
Painting the Avatar.

161
00:09:12,029 --> 00:09:13,613
That's easy enough.

162
00:09:13,697 --> 00:09:15,573
There's another one.

163
00:09:15,658 --> 00:09:17,700
Well, I'll make an adjustment
here and...

164
00:09:18,452 --> 00:09:19,786
There's more.

165
00:09:19,870 --> 00:09:21,162
I...

166
00:09:40,099 --> 00:09:43,309
Ooh! Heh heh!

167
00:09:44,979 --> 00:09:47,564
I can't believe I got beat up
by a bunch of girls.

168
00:09:51,652 --> 00:09:52,652
Sorry, ladies.

169
00:09:52,736 --> 00:09:54,696
Didn't mean to interrupt
your dance lesson.

170
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:57,073
I was just looking for somewhere
to get a little workout.

171
00:09:57,157 --> 00:09:59,576
Well, you're in the right place.

172
00:09:59,994 --> 00:10:01,536
Sorry about yesterday.

173
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:03,913
I didn't know
you were friends with the Avatar.

174
00:10:03,998 --> 00:10:05,039
It's all right.

175
00:10:05,124 --> 00:10:06,499
I mean, normally I'd hold a grudge,

176
00:10:06,584 --> 00:10:09,294
but seeing as you guys are a bunch
of girls, I'll make an exception.

177
00:10:09,378 --> 00:10:11,004
I should hope so.

178
00:10:11,088 --> 00:10:13,673
A big, strong man like you,

179
00:10:13,757 --> 00:10:15,216
we wouldn't stand a chance.

180
00:10:15,384 --> 00:10:16,885
True, but don't feel bad.

181
00:10:16,969 --> 00:10:19,095
After all, I'm the best warrior
in my village.

182
00:10:19,305 --> 00:10:21,556
Wow. Best warrior?

183
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:23,057
In your whole village?

184
00:10:23,142 --> 00:10:26,019
Maybe you'd be kind enough
to give us a little demonstration.

185
00:10:27,146 --> 00:10:28,980
Well, I mean, I...

186
00:10:29,064 --> 00:10:30,356
Come on, girls,

187
00:10:30,441 --> 00:10:32,025
wouldn't you like him
to show us some moves?

188
00:10:33,694 --> 00:10:35,028
Well, if that's what you want,

189
00:10:35,112 --> 00:10:36,446
I'd be happy to.

190
00:10:36,530 --> 00:10:39,073
All right, you stand over there.

191
00:10:39,158 --> 00:10:41,701
Now, this may be a little tough,

192
00:10:41,785 --> 00:10:43,494
but try to block me.

193
00:10:46,790 --> 00:10:48,041
Good.

194
00:10:48,125 --> 00:10:49,626
Of course, I was going easy on you.

195
00:10:49,752 --> 00:10:50,752
Of course.

196
00:10:50,961 --> 00:10:52,587
Let's see if you can handle this!

197
00:10:52,671 --> 00:10:53,671
Ouch!

198
00:10:55,716 --> 00:10:56,758
That does it!

199
00:11:09,355 --> 00:11:11,272
Anything else you want to teach us?

200
00:11:16,862 --> 00:11:19,530
There she is, girls,
me in a past life.

201
00:11:22,034 --> 00:11:24,661
You were pretty.

202
00:11:24,745 --> 00:11:26,704
Excuse me for a second, ladies.

203
00:11:30,167 --> 00:11:31,209
Good.

204
00:11:31,293 --> 00:11:32,794
Can you help me carry this
back to the room?

205
00:11:32,878 --> 00:11:34,087
It's a little heavy.

206
00:11:34,171 --> 00:11:35,463
Actually, I can't right now.

207
00:11:35,547 --> 00:11:36,547
What do you mean, you can't?

208
00:11:36,632 --> 00:11:39,050
I promised the girls
I'd give them a ride on Appa.

209
00:11:39,134 --> 00:11:40,134
Why don't you come with us?

210
00:11:40,219 --> 00:11:41,219
It'll be fun.

211
00:11:41,345 --> 00:11:43,388
Watching you show off
for a bunch of girls

212
00:11:43,472 --> 00:11:44,597
does not sound like fun.

213
00:11:44,974 --> 00:11:47,392
Well, neither does
carrying your basket.

214
00:11:47,476 --> 00:11:48,977
It's not my basket.

215
00:11:49,061 --> 00:11:50,853
These supplies are for our trip.

216
00:11:50,938 --> 00:11:52,814
I told you,
we have to leave Kyoshi soon.

217
00:11:53,023 --> 00:11:54,857
I don't want to leave Kyoshi yet.

218
00:11:54,942 --> 00:11:56,484
I can't put my finger on it,

219
00:11:56,568 --> 00:11:58,903
but there's something
I really like about this place.

220
00:12:00,364 --> 00:12:03,616
What's taking you so long, Aangie?

221
00:12:03,701 --> 00:12:04,701
Aangie?

222
00:12:04,785 --> 00:12:06,244
Just a second, Koko.

223
00:12:06,328 --> 00:12:07,912
Simple monk?

224
00:12:07,997 --> 00:12:09,956
I thought you promised
me this Avatar stuff

225
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,040
wouldn't go to your head.

226
00:12:11,208 --> 00:12:13,209
It didn't. You know what I think?

227
00:12:13,293 --> 00:12:15,753
You just don't want to come
because you're jealous.

228
00:12:15,838 --> 00:12:17,547
Jealous? Of what?

229
00:12:17,631 --> 00:12:19,882
Jealous that we're having
so much fun without you.

230
00:12:19,967 --> 00:12:21,175
That's ridiculous.

231
00:12:21,301 --> 00:12:22,593
It is a little ridiculous,

232
00:12:22,678 --> 00:12:23,678
but I understand.

233
00:12:36,025 --> 00:12:37,775
Hey, Suki.

234
00:12:38,652 --> 00:12:40,403
Hoping for another dance lesson?

235
00:12:40,487 --> 00:12:41,654
No, I...

236
00:12:41,739 --> 00:12:42,864
Well, let me explain.

237
00:12:42,948 --> 00:12:45,366
Spit it out. What do you want?

238
00:12:48,370 --> 00:12:50,913
I would be honored
if you would teach me.

239
00:12:50,998 --> 00:12:52,540
Even if I'm a girl?

240
00:12:52,624 --> 00:12:54,667
I'm sorry if I insulted you earlier.

241
00:12:54,752 --> 00:12:55,793
I was wrong.

242
00:12:55,878 --> 00:12:58,046
We normally don't teach outsiders,

243
00:12:58,130 --> 00:12:59,922
let alone boys.

244
00:13:00,007 --> 00:13:01,382
Please make an exception.

245
00:13:01,467 --> 00:13:02,508
I won't let you down.

246
00:13:02,634 --> 00:13:06,262
All right, but you have to follow
all of our traditions.

247
00:13:06,346 --> 00:13:07,388
Of course.

248
00:13:07,473 --> 00:13:09,640
And I mean all of them.

249
00:13:11,310 --> 00:13:12,643
Do I really have to wear this?

250
00:13:12,853 --> 00:13:14,812
It feels a little... Girly.

251
00:13:14,897 --> 00:13:16,522
It's a warrior's uniform.

252
00:13:16,607 --> 00:13:17,732
You should be proud.

253
00:13:17,816 --> 00:13:19,525
The silk thread symbolizes

254
00:13:19,610 --> 00:13:21,903
the brave blood
that flows through our veins.

255
00:13:21,987 --> 00:13:23,654
The gold insignia represents

256
00:13:23,739 --> 00:13:25,323
the honor of the warrior's heart.

257
00:13:27,034 --> 00:13:28,659
Bravery and honor.

258
00:13:28,744 --> 00:13:29,952
Hey, Sokka.

259
00:13:30,037 --> 00:13:31,162
Nice dress.

260
00:13:41,090 --> 00:13:45,176
Katara, remember how
the unagi almost got me yesterday?

261
00:13:45,260 --> 00:13:46,302
Yeah.

262
00:13:46,386 --> 00:13:48,221
Well, I'm going to go ride it now.

263
00:13:48,305 --> 00:13:49,931
It's going to be real dangerous.

264
00:13:50,015 --> 00:13:51,182
Good for you.

265
00:13:51,266 --> 00:13:52,308
You're not going to stop me?

266
00:13:52,392 --> 00:13:53,684
Nope. Have fun.

267
00:13:53,769 --> 00:13:55,019
I will. Great.

268
00:13:55,104 --> 00:13:56,145
I know it's great.

269
00:13:56,230 --> 00:13:57,271
Well, I'm glad you know.

270
00:13:57,356 --> 00:13:58,439
-I'm glad you're glad.
-Good!

271
00:13:58,524 --> 00:13:59,524
Fine!

272
00:14:06,865 --> 00:14:08,783
You're not going to master it
in one day.

273
00:14:08,867 --> 00:14:10,243
Even I'm not that good.

274
00:14:10,494 --> 00:14:11,994
I think I'm starting to get it.

275
00:14:21,630 --> 00:14:23,256
It's not about strength.

276
00:14:24,508 --> 00:14:27,510
Our technique is about using
your opponent's force against them.

277
00:14:27,594 --> 00:14:28,845
Loosen up.

278
00:14:28,929 --> 00:14:31,973
Think of the fan as an extension
of your arm.

279
00:14:32,057 --> 00:14:33,766
Wait for an opening and then...

280
00:14:39,022 --> 00:14:41,315
I fell on purpose
to make you feel better.

281
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:42,400
I got you!

282
00:14:42,484 --> 00:14:43,484
Admit I got you!

283
00:14:45,362 --> 00:14:47,613
Ok, it was a lucky shot.

284
00:14:47,823 --> 00:14:49,782
Let's see if you can do it again.

285
00:14:56,582 --> 00:14:58,249
What's taking so long?

286
00:14:58,333 --> 00:15:00,710
I'm sure it will be here any second.

287
00:15:02,296 --> 00:15:05,006
Um, what about this?

288
00:15:05,090 --> 00:15:06,549
Not that again.

289
00:15:06,633 --> 00:15:07,717
Boring.

290
00:15:07,801 --> 00:15:09,218
Where's unagi?

291
00:15:09,428 --> 00:15:10,469
It's getting late.

292
00:15:10,721 --> 00:15:12,054
Where are you going?

293
00:15:12,139 --> 00:15:13,139
Don't leave!

294
00:15:13,515 --> 00:15:14,682
Sorry, Aang!

295
00:15:14,766 --> 00:15:15,933
Maybe next time!

296
00:15:21,064 --> 00:15:22,565
Katara, you showed up!

297
00:15:22,649 --> 00:15:24,942
I wanted to make sure you were safe.

298
00:15:25,027 --> 00:15:26,277
You really had me worried.

299
00:15:26,528 --> 00:15:28,446
Back there you acted like
you didn't care.

300
00:15:28,530 --> 00:15:30,031
I'm sorry.

301
00:15:30,115 --> 00:15:31,365
Me, too.

302
00:15:31,450 --> 00:15:33,618
I did let all that attention
go to my head.

303
00:15:33,702 --> 00:15:35,203
I was being a jerk.

304
00:15:35,287 --> 00:15:36,537
Well, get out of the water

305
00:15:36,622 --> 00:15:38,456
before you catch a cold, you big jerk!

306
00:15:39,625 --> 00:15:40,791
On my way!

307
00:16:27,756 --> 00:16:29,173
Hang on, Aang!

308
00:16:29,258 --> 00:16:30,424
Aah!

309
00:16:39,851 --> 00:16:40,851
Aang!

310
00:17:09,131 --> 00:17:10,131
Zuko!

311
00:17:24,563 --> 00:17:26,105
I want the Avatar alive.

312
00:17:42,539 --> 00:17:43,956
Wake up, Aang.

313
00:17:52,049 --> 00:17:53,049
Katara.

314
00:17:55,052 --> 00:17:56,927
Don't ride the unagi.

315
00:17:57,012 --> 00:17:58,429
Not fun.

316
00:18:05,145 --> 00:18:06,354
Not bad.

317
00:18:08,065 --> 00:18:10,066
Fire bandits have landed
on our shores.

318
00:18:10,150 --> 00:18:11,859
Girls, come quickly!

319
00:18:11,943 --> 00:18:13,736
Hey, I'm not a...

320
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:15,488
Whatever.

321
00:18:21,870 --> 00:18:23,120
Come out, Avatar.

322
00:18:23,205 --> 00:18:24,622
You can't hide from me forever.

323
00:18:30,170 --> 00:18:31,379
Find him.

324
00:19:08,667 --> 00:19:10,376
I guess training's over.

325
00:19:22,556 --> 00:19:24,014
Nice try, Avatar,

326
00:19:24,099 --> 00:19:26,434
but these little girls can't save you.

327
00:19:26,852 --> 00:19:28,561
Hey, over here!

328
00:19:30,439 --> 00:19:31,564
Finally.

329
00:20:11,396 --> 00:20:12,688
Get inside.

330
00:20:16,776 --> 00:20:18,486
Look what I brought to this place.

331
00:20:18,570 --> 00:20:19,695
It's not your fault.

332
00:20:19,779 --> 00:20:21,071
Yes, it is.

333
00:20:21,156 --> 00:20:23,908
These people got their town destroyed
trying to protect me.

334
00:20:23,992 --> 00:20:25,284
Then let's get out of here.

335
00:20:25,368 --> 00:20:27,328
Zuko will leave Kyoshi to follow us.

336
00:20:27,412 --> 00:20:28,829
I know it feels wrong to run,

337
00:20:29,039 --> 00:20:30,247
but I think it's the only way.

338
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:32,917
I'll call Appa.

339
00:20:39,591 --> 00:20:41,425
There's no time to say good-bye.

340
00:20:41,510 --> 00:20:42,801
What about "I'm sorry"?

341
00:20:42,886 --> 00:20:43,886
For what?

342
00:20:44,179 --> 00:20:45,179
I treated you like a girl

343
00:20:45,263 --> 00:20:47,056
when I should have
treated you like a warrior.

344
00:20:47,265 --> 00:20:48,682
I am a warrior...

345
00:20:50,644 --> 00:20:52,311
But I'm a girl, too.

346
00:20:54,397 --> 00:20:55,523
Now get out of here.

347
00:20:55,607 --> 00:20:56,941
We'll hold them off.

348
00:21:00,904 --> 00:21:02,404
Appa, yip yip!

349
00:21:05,158 --> 00:21:06,492
Back to the ship!

350
00:21:06,576 --> 00:21:08,202
Don't lose sight of them!

351
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:14,416
I know it's hard,
but you did the right thing.

352
00:21:14,501 --> 00:21:17,211
Zuko would've destroyed
the whole place if we stayed.

353
00:21:17,295 --> 00:21:18,754
They're going to be ok, Aang.

354
00:21:22,217 --> 00:21:23,676
What are you doing?

355
00:22:00,547 --> 00:22:02,131
Thank you, Avatar.

356
00:22:03,675 --> 00:22:05,342
I know, I know,

357
00:22:05,427 --> 00:22:07,052
that was stupid and dangerous.

358
00:22:07,262 --> 00:22:09,179
Yes, it was.
